    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4564A                 REVISED 3/22/23\n\nSPONSOR: GALLIVAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Trooper William P. Keane Memorial\nBridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo honor the life and ultimate sacrifice of New York State Police Troop-\ner William P. Keane by naming the State route 179 bridge over Interstate\n90 in the Town of Hamburg the \"Trooper William P. Keane Memorial\nBridge\".\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one adds a new section to the highway law designating State\nroute 179 bridge over Interstate 90 in the Town of Hamburg, Erie County\nas the \"Trooper William P Keane Memorial Bridge\".\n\nSection 2 requires the chairperson of the New York State Thruway Author-\nity to provide for the installation and maintenance of adequate signage.\n\nSection 3 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTrooper William P Keane, a twenty-six veteran of the New York State\nPolice, passed away on August 23, 2013 while on-duty with the New York\nState Police at the Commercial Vehicle Safety Alliance Conference in\nSalt Lake City, UT.\n\nOriginally, from Western New York, specifically South Buffalo, Trooper\nKeane served in the United States Navy prior to becoming a New York\nState Trooper and was renowned for his dedication and knowledgeable\nservice with Commercial Vehicle Enforcement Laws. It is fitting that we\nhonor his life and ultimate sacrifice by naming the bridge over I-90 in\nthe Town of Hamburg the \"Trooper William P. Keane Memorial Bridge\".\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
